 event replays: each event is forecast by models retrained without that event (+- 7 days), so those models may have learned from floods that happened after the replayed one. Events in the test period (e2024a, e2024b, e2026) use the time-split models directly. Repeat crossings within 72 h count as one flood. An EA Flood Warning counts as in force from its issue time until 24 h after its last Update, and is scored on the same hours and rules as our trigger. Lead versus the EA compares first messages within the same flood. Arrival error uses the forecast issued 24 h before the first crossing and is blank when that forecast did not reach 50%. Abingdon Rd shares the EA warning area 061FWF23NwBotley with Botley, so its lead versus the EA is measured against the Botley warning, while its own gauge crosses later. Each spot's warn-at level (warnAt) was chosen on the validation flood replays only (issue times before 2021-10-01: e2007, e2012, e2014, e2021) by one fixed rule, then frozen and scored on the test events. Few events, so intervals are wide.","officialOutcome":{"osney":{"hits":5,"misses":2,"falseAlarms":0,"meanLeadH":24.33},"botley":{"hits":8,"misses":0,"falseAlarms":0,"meanLeadH":37.84},"abingdonrd":{"hits":8,"misses":0,"falseAlarms":0,"meanLeadH":41.99},"cherwell":{"hits":3,"misses":4,"falseAlarms":1,"meanLeadH":2.99}},"warnAt":{"osney":{"pStar":0.5,"rule":"Lowest p* in 0.1-0.9 with at most 1 false alarm in every validation flood replay (issue times before 2021-10-01: e2007, e2012, e2014, e2021); 0.5 if none qualifies. Chosen before looking at the test period.","validation":{"events":["e2007","e2012","e2014","e2021"],"hits":6,"misses":0,"falseAlarms":2,"meanLeadH":17.83,"meanLeadVsOfficialH":2.34},"test":{"events":["e2024a","e2024b","e2026"],"hits":1,"misses":0,"falseAlarms":0,"meanLeadH":11.0,"meanLeadVsOfficialH":1.5},"atDefault":{"pStar":0.5,"validation":{"events":["e2007","e2012","e2014","e2021"],"hits":6,"misses":0,"falseAlarms":2,"meanLeadH":17.83,"meanLeadVs